BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-international-collaborative-projects-heritage-institutes-2026
 @artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260910
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260911
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: International Collaborative Projects with
  Heritage Institutes (September 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:This scheme funds cultural heritage institutions in the Netherl
 ands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom that want to collaborate with f
 oreign heritage institutions on research projects in shared collection are
 as\, including art historical and provenance research. A development phase
  can also be funded\, covering travel\, accommodation and presentation cos
 ts while the collaboration is being shaped. CONDITIONS: the applicant inst
 itution must be publicly accessible and manage nationally significant cult
 ural heritage\; it must partner with comparable institutions abroad\; the 
 research must be presented by both the Dutch and the international partner
 s\; the applicant must contribute significantly to financing the project\;
  and the international partners' share of costs must be proportional to th
 e Mondriaan Fund grant. AMOUNTS: up to 40% of variable project costs for t
 he main project\, or up to 70% of variable costs capped at EUR 15\,000 for
  development research. APPLY through the Mondriaan Fund online application
  system after registering an account. Deadline 10 September 2026 before 16
 :00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time (an earlier 28 May 2026 round has pa
 ssed).\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\nLocation: Applicant institutions m
 ust be based in the Netherlands or the Caribbean part of the Kingdom\; the
  partner institutions are abroad.\nAward: Determined per application. Up t
 o 40% of variable project costs. For a development research phase\, up to 
 70% of variable costs capped at EUR 15\,000\, covering travel\, accommodat
 ion and presentation costs. The applicant must contribute significantly to
  the project financing\, and the international partners' cost share must b
 e proportional to the Mondriaan Fund grant. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Project-based research collaboration. Two annual rounds\; this card cover
 s the 10 September 2026 deadline.\n\nMore: https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/e
 n/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international-collaborative-projects-with-herit
 age-institutes/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/international
 -collaborative-projects-with-heritage-institutes/?utm_source=artificialnou
 veaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant institutions must be based in the Netherlands or the Car
 ibbean part of the Kingdom\; the partner institutions are abroad.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mondriaan-heritage-innovation-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260918
SUMMARY:Deadline: Mondriaan Fund: Heritage Innovation (September 2026 round
 )
DESCRIPTION:Heritage Innovation funds projects and research tracks that con
 tribute to substantive innovation in the heritage sector. Examples given b
 y the fund include developing new narratives about cultural heritage\, str
 engthening regional collaboration across the sector\, redesigning how a co
 llection is presented\, and feasibility studies on technological applicati
 ons such as AI or gamification\, which makes this one of the more tech-adj
 acent Mondriaan schemes. WHO CAN APPLY: museums and collection-holding cul
 tural heritage institutions\, including archives\, in the Netherlands and 
 the Caribbean part of the Kingdom. Cultural organisations in the heritage 
 sector may also apply if they collaborate with one or more collection-hold
 ing institutions. All applicants must be non-profit\, not-for-profit entit
 ies. NOT FUNDED: fixed costs\, restoration\, building museums\, or regular
  operations. CONDITIONS: institutions must subscribe to the Fair Practice 
 Code\, the Culture Governance Code and the Diversity and Inclusion Code\, 
 and must pay visual artists fairly where artists are involved. AMOUNTS: pr
 ojects get up to 40% of variable project-related costs on a minimum projec
 t budget of EUR 25\,000\; research tracks get up to 70% of costs capped at
  EUR 15\,000 with no minimum budget. APPLY through the Mondriaan Fund onli
 ne system after registering an account. Deadline 17 September 2026 before 
 16:00 Dutch time / 10:00 Caribbean time.\n\nOrganisation: Mondriaan Fund\n
 Location: Museums and collection-holding heritage institutions in the Neth
 erlands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.\nAward: Projects: up to 40%
  of variable project-related costs\, with a minimum project budget of EUR 
 25\,000. Research tracks: up to 70% of costs\, capped at EUR 15\,000\, wit
 h no minimum budget. No application fee.\nDuration: Project or research tr
 ack. This card covers the 17 September 2026 deadline.\n\nMore: https://www
 .mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/heritage-innovation/?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mondriaanfonds.nl/en/apply-for-a-grant/grants/heritage-inno
 vation/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Museums and collection-holding heritage institutions in the Nether
 lands and the Caribbean part of the Kingdom.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nwo-ssh-xs-2026-round-3@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260916
SUMMARY:Deadline: NWO: SSH Open Competition XS 2026 - Round 3
DESCRIPTION:Small curiosity-driven research grants in the social sciences a
 nd humanities\, awarded by the Dutch Research Council (NWO). Round 3 of th
 e 2026 SSH Open Competition XS closes 15 September 2026\, 14:00 CEST. Up t
 o EUR 50\,000 per project to enable researchers to pursue novel\, explorat
 ory and high-risk ideas without the constraints of larger themed calls. EL
 IGIBILITY: academic researchers with an institutional affiliation at a Dut
 ch university or recognised Dutch knowledge institute. Proposals are asses
 sed on scientific quality and the potential for renewal of social-sciences
  and humanities research. Round 3 details and the dedicated application pa
 ge will be published by NWO closer to the deadline\; the linked page is th
 e most recent SSH XS round\, which is the same scheme.\n\nOrganisation: Du
 tch Research Council (NWO)\nLocation: Netherlands (applicants must be acad
 emic researchers affiliated to a Dutch knowledge institution)\nAward: Up t
 o EUR 50\,000 per project\nDuration: Project-based\, typically 12-24 month
 s\n\nMore: https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/ssh-open-competition-xs-2026-round-
 3?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.nwo.nl/en/calls/ssh-open-competition-xs-2026-round-3?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands (applicants must be academic researchers affiliated to
  a Dutch knowledge institution)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kb-researcher-in-residence-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Deadline: KB Researcher-in-Residence (RiR) 2027
DESCRIPTION:ELIGIBILITY: two Researcher-in-Residence positions in 2027. Ope
 n to early-career researchers of any discipline (data science\, social sci
 ence\, computer science\, humanities) who are currently working on a PhD o
 r within 5 years of their PhD end date. You must have\, or be able to secu
 re\, an affiliation with a Dutch university or research institute willing 
 to second you\; external PhD students may use the funding to obtain such a
  contract. Your project must make use of one or more of the KB digital col
 lections and you must be able to work with primarily Dutch data. You must 
 be available at 0.5 FTE over 6 months and able to spend two days a week on
 -site at the KB in The Hague. COLLECTIONS: over 130 million digitized page
 s of newspapers\, magazines\, radio bulletins and books from 1470 onward (
 via Delpher and DBNL)\, a born-digital web collection of more than 23\,000
  websites\, ground-truth and derived datasets on the KB Lab\, and metadata
  including Linked Data. APPLY: use the official proposal template and subm
 it a single PDF by 27 September 2026 to dh@kb.nl\, after reading the call'
 s terms and conditions\; questions to dh@kb.nl. TIMELINE: deadline 27 Sept
 ember 2026\; internal eligibility review followed by an external committee
  review\; outcome notified November 2026\; residencies start Q1 and Q3 202
 7. DISCIPLINES: digital humanities / data science / computational research
  with cultural-heritage collections. NOTE: the output is usually a dataset
  or tool prototype hosted on the KB Lab\; you agree to share results via b
 log posts on the KB Lab and to publish resulting tools or data under an op
 en license within 6 months of the residency. Proposals should align with t
 he KB Research Agenda or the Cultural AI Lab.\n\nOrganisation: KB\, Nation
 al Library of the Netherlands\nLocation: The Hague\, Netherlands (two days
  per week on-site at the KB premises)\nAward: Secondment at 0.5 FTE for 6 
 months based on your current salary\, up to EUR 5\,590 gross per month for
  a full-time-equivalent position\, plus travel expenses\, office facilitie
 s\, and support from a research software engineer\, research advisor\, and
  collection and data specialists. No application fee.\nDuration: 6 months 
 at 0.5 FTE (two days per week on-site)\; two positions in 2027\, starting 
 Q1 and Q3\n\nMore: https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir
 -2027?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://lab.kb.nl/news/call-kb-researcher-residence-rir-2027?utm_source
 =artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:The Hague\, Netherlands (two days per week on-site at the KB premi
 ses)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hva-digital-life-researcher-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260730
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260731
SUMMARY:Deadline: Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences: Digital Life Re
 searcher (Embodied AI Rehabilitation Agents)
DESCRIPTION:A junior researcher post in the Digital Life research group at 
 the Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences\, working on embodied AI reha
 bilitation agents that support patients during rehabilitation and recovery
  in everyday life. The programme sits at the intersection of human-centred
  AI\, digital health and rehabilitation technology\, and the role is unusu
 ally hands-on for a research job: co-designing rehabilitation technologies
  with patients and healthcare professionals\, building interactive prototy
 pes with sensing technologies and embodied interaction\, running user-cent
 red evaluations in real-world living lab settings\, and contributing to sc
 ientific reports and presentations. REQUIREMENTS: a master's degree in hum
 an-computer interaction\, industrial design\, computer science\, software 
 engineering\, AI or a related field\; demonstrated research experience inc
 luding co-design and evaluation with diverse stakeholders\; experience des
 igning interactive prototypes with sensing or embodied systems\; sensor da
 ta collection\, processing and analysis skills\; and programming in Python
 \, JavaScript or comparable languages. Excellent written and spoken Englis
 h is required and Dutch proficiency is preferred. Apply with a CV and moti
 vation letter through the application portal. Contact: Bin Yu (b.yu@hva.nl
 \, 0638347028) or vacatures@hva.nl. Closes 30 July 2026.\n\nOrganisation: 
 Amsterdam University of Applied Sciences (Hogeschool van Amsterdam)\nLocat
 ion: Amsterdam\, Netherlands (Weesperzijde campus)\, on site\nAward: EUR 3
 \,064.08 to 4\,084.93 gross per month for 40 hours per week\, plus an 8.3 
 percent year-end bonus and 8 percent holiday allowance.\nDuration: Full-ti
 me\, 40 hours per week\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/3
 62580/digital-life-onderzoeksmedewerker-researcher/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362580/digital-life-onderzoeks
 medewerker-researcher/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=re
 ferral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands (Weesperzijde campus)\, on site
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rug-lecturer-arts-culture-media-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Groningen: Lecturer 4\, Arts\, Culture and 
 Media
DESCRIPTION:A one-year teaching appointment in the Faculty of Arts at the U
 niversity of Groningen\, covering courses across the BA in Arts\, Culture 
 and Media and the Popular Music and Sonic Cultures master's track. Teachin
 g spans audiovisual arts\, popular music and arts management at both under
 graduate and postgraduate level. This is a teaching-weighted post rather t
 han a research one\, so it suits practitioners who want a formal academic 
 foothold in audiovisual and sonic culture without committing to a research
  track. REQUIREMENTS: a research master's in an appropriate arts disciplin
 e\, undergraduate teaching experience\, and English at C1 (CEFR). PREFERRE
 D: a PhD in an appropriate arts discipline\, a BKO or UTQ teaching qualifi
 cation\, postgraduate teaching experience\, musicology expertise\, Dutch a
 t B2\, and familiarity with the Dutch higher education system. Apply throu
 gh the AcademicTransfer posting (vacancy ID V26.2320-EN). Closes 15 August
  2026\; appointment starts 1 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University o
 f Groningen\, Faculty of Arts\nLocation: Groningen\, Netherlands (Broerstr
 aat 5)\nAward: EUR 3\,706 to 5\,760 gross per month at 1.0 FTE (the post i
 s 0.8 FTE)\, plus standard Dutch university holiday and year-end allowance
 s.\nDuration: Temporary\, 12-month fixed-term appointment at 0.8 FTE\, sta
 rting 1 September 2026\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/3
 62915/lecturer-4-arts-culture-and-media/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrant
 desk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362915/lecturer-4-arts-culture
 -and-media/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Groningen\, Netherlands (Broerstraat 5)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twente-postdoc-conversational-ai-cultural-heritage-2026@artificialnouve
 au.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Twente: Postdoc\, Multimodal Conversational
  AI for Cultural Heritage
DESCRIPTION:A postdoctoral position in the Human Media Interaction group at
  the University of Twente on the project 'Balancing Personalisation and Po
 lyvocality: Dialogic Interaction for Open-mindedness and Empathy in Conver
 sational AI'. The work develops and evaluates multimodal conversational ag
 ents for museum settings that hold personalisation in tension with exposur
 e to plural perspectives\, rather than optimising for engagement alone. Ta
 sks include building models that use gaze\, speech and dialogue data to in
 fer visitor engagement and openness\, designing adaptive dialogue strategi
 es\, running VR-based user studies\, and publishing in strong venues. Of t
 he current Dutch academic postings this is the closest thing to a funded c
 reative-technologist brief: museum interpretation\, multimodal sensing and
  dialogue design in one role. REQUIREMENTS: a PhD in computer science\, AI
 \, HCI or a related field\; experience with conversational AI\, dialogue s
 ystems or adaptive systems\; experience running empirical research\, prefe
 rably user studies\; strong analytical and academic writing skills\; and e
 xcellent English. Apply with a CV including publications\, a motivation le
 tter and two academic references. Contact: Shenghui Wang (shenghui.wang@ut
 wente.nl). NOTE: the AcademicTransfer listing page shows a 16 August 2026 
 deadline while the detail page states 17 August 2026\, so treat 16 August 
 as the effective cut-off.\n\nOrganisation: University of Twente\, Human Me
 dia Interaction group\nLocation: Enschede\, Netherlands\nAward: EUR 3\,546
  to 5\,538 gross per month for 40 hours per week (8 salary steps\, dependi
 ng on experience)\, plus standard Dutch university holiday and year-end al
 lowances.\nDuration: One year\, renewable for a further two years subject 
 to positive evaluation\; 40 hours per week\n\nMore: https://www.academictr
 ansfer.com/en/jobs/362707/postdoc-position-on-multimodal-conversational-ai
 -for-cultural-heritage/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=r
 eferral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362707/postdoc-position-on-mul
 timodal-conversational-ai-for-cultural-heritage/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Enschede\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:twente-postdoc-llms4eu-ethics-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260825
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Twente: Postdoc\, Ethics and Epistemology o
 f LLMs4EU (17 months)
DESCRIPTION:A postdoctoral position in the Philosophy section at the Univer
 sity of Twente\, part of the 4TU.Center for Ethics and Technology\, workin
 g on the ethics and epistemology strand (Work Package 6) of LLMs4EU. LLMs4
 EU is a European Commission funded initiative led by the Alliance for Lang
 uage Technologies\, spanning more than 20 countries\, to build large langu
 age models across all EU languages and preserve European linguistic and cu
 ltural diversity in the digital age while keeping the resulting tools comp
 liant with European values and legislation including the AI Act and the GD
 PR. TASKS: establish benchmarking frameworks that address legal and ethica
 l concerns\; develop guidelines for fine-tuning processes with an emphasis
  on preserving cultural heritage\; oversee ethics compliance and advise th
 e project ethics board\; and build frameworks that integrate ethical consi
 derations into LLM design. This is the tech-communication and language-pol
 itics end of AI research rather than a modelling job: the questions are wh
 ose language\, whose culture and whose norms get encoded when a continent 
 builds its own models. REQUIREMENTS: a doctorate in ethics\, philosophy\, 
 science and technology studies\, AI ethics\, computer science with an ethi
 cs focus\, or a related field\; demonstrated expertise in AI ethics and et
 hics compliance\; understanding of AI tool design and LLM development\; ap
 preciation for cultural diversity\; strong communication and organisationa
 l skills\; and professional English. Apply through the AcademicTransfer po
 sting. Closes 25 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University of Twente\, Phil
 osophy section / 4TU.Center for Ethics and Technology\nLocation: Enschede\
 , Netherlands\nAward: EUR 4\,241 to 5\,538 gross per month (scale 10\, ste
 ps 4 to 12) at 1.0 FTE\, plus 8 percent holiday allowance and an 8.3 perce
 nt year-end bonus.\nDuration: 17 months\, full-time (38 to 40 hours per we
 ek)\, with possible extension\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en
 /jobs/362444/postdoctoral-researcher-17-months-ethics-and-epistemology-of-
 llms4eu-design-data-and-deployment/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&
 utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362444/postdoctoral-researcher
 -17-months-ethics-and-epistemology-of-llms4eu-design-data-and-deployment/?
 utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Enschede\, Netherlands
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uva-phd-sound-of-disagreement-nordics-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260821
SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Amsterdam: PhD\, Protest and Political Spee
 ch in the Nordics 1930-1970 (Sound of Disagreement)
DESCRIPTION:Fully funded four-year PhD position within 'The Sound of Disagr
 eement: Embodied Histories of Political Speech 1800-present'\, an interdis
 ciplinary project on how political groups have argued in public and how di
 sagreement sounds. This sub-project covers Nordic labour movements and the
  articulation of protest from roughly 1930 to 1970\, explicitly working on
  the sonic practices of political debate and the mediatization of protest\
 , so it suits researchers with a sound studies\, media studies or oral his
 tory angle as much as historians. REQUIREMENTS: a master's degree in Histo
 ry\, European Studies\, Media Studies\, Nordic Studies or a related discip
 line\; fluency in Danish\, Finnish\, Norwegian or Swedish depending on the
  chosen case study\; professional English\; archival research skills\; and
  a collaborative disposition. Apply via the AcademicTransfer posting (vaca
 ncy number 15290) with a motivation letter\, CV and research statement. De
 adline 20 August 2026.\n\nOrganisation: University of Amsterdam (UvA)\, Fa
 culty of Humanities\, Department of European Studies\nLocation: Amsterdam\
 , Netherlands (Kloveniersburgwal 48)\nAward: EUR 3\,059 to 3\,881 gross pe
 r month at 38 hours per week\, on the Dutch university PhD scale\, plus 8 
 percent holiday allowance and 8.3 percent year-end bonus. No application f
 ee.\nDuration: 48 months full-time (16-month initial contract\, extended b
 y 32 months after a positive evaluation)\; preferred start 1 January 2027\
 n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362349/phd-position-on-p
 rotest-and-political-speech-in-the-nordics-1930-1970/?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362349/phd-position-on-protest
 -and-political-speech-in-the-nordics-1930-1970/?utm_source=artificialnouve
 augrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Amsterdam\, Netherlands (Kloveniersburgwal 48)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uu-phd-media-democracy-1970s-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260907
SUMMARY:Deadline: Utrecht University: PhD\, Media and Democracy in the 1970
 s (NWO Vidi project)
DESCRIPTION:Fully funded PhD position in the NWO-funded Vidi project 'Democ
 racy and the (de-)regulation of the media in Europe since the 1970s'\, whi
 ch reads the contestation and transformation of democracy in the last quar
 ter of the twentieth century through media governance. This sub-project ex
 amines how social movements\, pirate broadcasters and alternative media in
 itiatives challenged the public broadcasting monopoly across Western Europ
 e during the long 1970s\, drawing on archival research. REQUIREMENTS: a ma
 ster's degree in history or a related field\, a demonstrated interest in t
 he history of democracy and media governance\, professional English plus a
 t least one other European language\, archival research experience and a c
 ollaborative approach. Apply through the AcademicTransfer posting (vacancy
  number 5535). Project leader Dr Pepijn Corduwener (p.corduwener@uu.nl). D
 eadline 6 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: Utrecht University\, Faculty of
  Humanities\, Department of History and Art History\nLocation: Utrecht\, N
 etherlands (Drift 6)\nAward: EUR 3\,059 to 3\,881 gross per month at 36 to
  40 hours per week\, on the Dutch university PhD scale\, plus 8 percent ho
 liday allowance and 8.3 percent year-end bonus. No application fee.\nDurat
 ion: 18-month initial contract\, extended to four years after a positive f
 irst-year assessment\n\nMore: https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362
 200/phd-media-and-democracy-in-the-1970s/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugran
 tdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.academictransfer.com/en/jobs/362200/phd-media-and-democracy
 -in-the-1970s/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Utrecht\, Netherlands (Drift 6)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fondsbjp-dossiersubsidie-2026@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260914
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260915
SUMMARY:Deadline: Fonds BJP: Dossiersubsidie for Freelance Regional and Loc
 al Journalists (autumn 2026 round)
DESCRIPTION:The Dossiersubsidie is the Fonds BJP scheme for freelance regio
 nal and local journalists in the Netherlands who want to follow one subjec
 t properly rather than chase daily news\, funding up to EUR 19\,200 for si
 x months of sustained reporting on a single dossier. It is aimed at the ga
 p left by shrinking regional newsrooms\, where structural coverage of loca
 l government\, housing\, care or industry rarely gets paid time. ELIGIBILI
 TY: freelance journalists working in Dutch regional and local media only (
 staff journalists and national-only reporters are directed to the fund's o
 ther schemes). The fund also runs a year-round Vooronderzoekssubsidie of u
 p to EUR 8\,800 for preliminary research and a year-round Uitvoeringssubsi
 die of up to EUR 38\,600 for carrying out projects\, both open to all jour
 nalists. APPLICATION WINDOW: 17 August to 14 September 2026\, via the Fond
 s BJP subsidy portal. Online office hours on 8 September 2026\; questions 
 on 020 63 86 295.\n\nOrganisation: Fonds Bijzondere Journalistieke Project
 en (Fonds BJP)\nLocation: Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working 
 on Dutch regional and local reporting\nAward: Up to EUR 19\,200 for six mo
 nths of work on a single reporting dossier. No application fee.\nDuration:
  Six months of dedicated reporting on one subject area\n\nMore: https://ww
 w.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=
 referral
URL:https://www.fondsbjp.nl/subsidies/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdes
 k&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Netherlands\; for freelance journalists working on Dutch regional 
 and local reporting
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:glina3-open-call-type-language-visual-systems-2026@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260827T165714Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260812
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:Deadline: GLINA3: Open Call for a Collaborator Working with Type\, 
 Language and Visual Systems
DESCRIPTION:GLINA3 is an Amsterdam clay 3D printing and digital design stud
 io\, and it is looking for one collaborator to join a new research project
  at the intersection of typography\, language\, technology and material cu
 lture. They want an artist\, writer\, poet\, anthropologist or artistic re
 searcher whose existing practice already engages with type design\, typogr
 aphy\, writing systems\, visual language\, fonts and letterforms\, languag
 e technologies\, or the tools that shape how language is produced\, read o
 r translated. This is an unusually good fit for anyone working on the mach
 ine-readable side of language: the brief explicitly names language technol
 ogies and translation tooling alongside classical type design. ELIGIBILITY
 : individual practitioners with demonstrable work in one or more of the li
 sted areas. HOW TO APPLY: the studio asks for relevant work\, research\, p
 ublications or projects connected to type\, fonts\, writing systems\, visu
 al language or the tools that shape them\, and nothing else. Because the d
 eadline is tight they say Instagram DM is the fastest route\; you can also
  email a short introduction and one relevant project to office@glina3.nl. 
 NOTE: the fee is confirmed only if the project's own funding comes through
 \, so clarify terms before committing time.\n\nOrganisation: GLINA3\nLocat
 ion: Amsterdam\, Netherlands (studio is Amsterdam-based\; collaboration te
 rms not specified)\nAward: Paid collaboration. The studio states the fee w
 ill be confirmed upon successful funding\, so the amount is contingent and
  not published up front. No application fee.\nDuration: New collaborative 
